<title>SWEDEN: Orrefors group ups stake in Swedish glassmaker.</title>
<headline>Orrefors group ups stake in Swedish glassmaker.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>A consortium recently set up to buy Swedish glassware company Orrefors Kosta Boda said on Friday it had raised its stake to 99.1 percent.</p>
<p>The consortium, which is named Orrefors Kosta Boda Holding AB (OKB), is owned by Scandinavian Equity Partners, Swedish investment company Proventus AB and Danish luxury goods maker Royal Copenhagen A/S.</p>
<p>OKB had extended its takeover offer of 155 crowns a share until December 20 to complete the purchase of the prestigious glassmaker.</p>
<p>Orrefors Kosta Boda will cease trading on the Stockholm bourse on December 30.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
